    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Acetaminophen (Tylenol) or nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) like ibuprofen may provide some relief for chest discomfort, but they're not specific remedies for cardiac issues and should not be used as such. Numbness and tingling in your arm can sometimes be relieved by over-the-counter medications for neuropathy such as gabapentin or pregabalin, but again, they are not a substitute for proper diagnosis and treatment. It's very important to see a healthcare professional promptly to determine the exact cause of your symptoms and receive the appropriate care. In the meantime, try to manage your stress, stay hydrated, and avoid strenuous activities. If your symptoms worsen or if you experience shortness of breath, chest pain that radiates, or dizziness, seek medical attention immediately as these could be signs of a more serious condition.",
